","areaDesc":"Logan, CO; Phillips, CO; Sedgwick, CO; Washington, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.b5fc3fb0f4468acf2c3b7dde0584271abf13df82.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.b5fc3fb0f4468acf2c3b7dde0584271abf13df82.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Watch","headline":"Flood Watch issued August 15 at 7:17PM MDT until August 15 at 10:00PM MDT by NWS Denver CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be\npossible.\n\n* WHERE...Portions of east central and northeast Colorado, including\neastern Elbert, Lincoln, Washington, Sedgwick, and Phillips\nCounties.\n\n* WHEN...Until 10 PM MDT this evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.\nFlooding may occur in poor drainage and urban areas.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Additional thunderstorms and heavy rainfall this evening,\ncombined with the heavy rainfall from the past 3 days, will bring\na threat for flash flooding this afternoon and evening. Stronger\nstorms will be capable of producing 1 to 2 inches of rain in 30\nminutes, with isolated areas receiving storm totals of 3+ inches.","ends":"2026-08-15T22:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"North and Northeast Elbert County Below 6000 Feet/North Lincoln County; Southeast Elbert County Below 6000 Feet/South Lincoln County; Washington County; Sedgwick County; Phillips County","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.519c2be3a0730d8deea55189560ee1a22a98ac43.002.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.519c2be3a0730d8deea55189560ee1a22a98ac43.002.1"},{"event":"Severe Thunderstorm Watch","headline":"Severe Thunderstorm Watch issued August 15 at 6:49PM MDT until August 15 at 9:00PM MDT by NWS Denver CO","description":"SEVERE THUNDERSTORM WATCH 584 REMAINS VALID UNTIL 9 PM MDT THIS\nEVENING FOR THE FOLLOWING AREAS\n\nIN COLORADO THIS WATCH INCLUDES 3 COUNTIES\n\nIN EAST CENTRAL COLORADO\n\nLINCOLN\n\nIN NORTH